+# HAOS WebUI branding and updater policy
+
+This document records the safe branding boundary for the HAOS deployment of the
+WebUI. It is intentionally explicit about what was verified and what was not.
+
+## Branding audit
+
+- The browser shell identifies itself as **HAOS WebUI** in `static/index.html`.
+- The PWA manifest identifies itself as **HAOS WebUI** and its icon references
+  resolve to files shipped in `static/`.
+- The favicon family (`favicon.svg`, `favicon-512.svg`, PNG variants, ICO, and
+  Apple touch icon) is existing repository content. No external asset was added
+  by this audit.
+- The repository history attributes the current icon family to commit
+  `5eff106e` ("Swap brand to new cyan caduceus..."). The source/licence of that
+  artwork is not independently verified here. Therefore this change does not
+  replace, redraw, or redistribute it.
+- `LICENSE` remains the repository's MIT license for the WebUI. It is not used
+  as proof that the artwork has a separate third-party license. A future asset
+  replacement requires a source URL, license evidence, and an explicit record
+  of the asset's provenance before it is merged.
+
+The product identity remains distinct from the runtime assistant identity:
+branding the shell as HAOS WebUI does not rename the Hermes assistant shown in
+conversation settings or welcome copy.
+
+## Updater policy
+
+The policy has two independent controls:
+
+1. `allow_agent_updates: false` (default) protects the HAOS-managed Agent
+   checkout at `/usr/local/lib/haos-agent` from WebUI-initiated Agent mutations.
+   The guard covers normal update, force update, and lock-recovery mutation
+   entry points. It fails closed when settings cannot be read. Setting the
+   value to the literal boolean `true` is an explicit operator opt-in.
+2. `ignore_agent_updates` controls Agent update discovery/fetches and notices.
+   It does **not** control WebUI updates. When it is false (the default), the
+   WebUI continues checking both repositories; when true, Agent checks are
+   omitted while WebUI checks continue.
+
+Normal WebUI updates remain available regardless of the Agent mutation policy:
+`target=webui` is not classified as the managed Agent boundary and continues to
+use the existing WebUI updater path. Docker/no-git installs remain manual-update
+or informational paths as determined by the existing updater behavior.
+
+This policy does not authorize direct edits to the Agent checkout, automatic
+restart of a stale WebUI process, or deletion of Git lock files. Those remain
+separate safety boundaries documented in `docs/troubleshooting.md`.
+
+## Verification record
+
+Verified in the source tree:
+
+- `static/index.html` and `static/manifest.json` contain the HAOS WebUI shell
+  identity.
+- The manifest's local icon paths exist.
+- Existing updater regression tests cover the protected managed-Agent path,
+  explicit opt-in, skipped Agent checks, and the unaffected WebUI path.
+
+Not verified: independent copyright/licence provenance for the existing icon
+artwork, and a live browser/PWA install against a deployed server.
